# cat: copies input to output until end of input.
# A counter-clockwise ring. The origin is south of the black bit,
# so the walk starts there heading north.
#
#   green -- red --- orange
#     |       |        |
#   pink -- white -- black   <- start
#     |
#   brown  (exit)
black      0  1000   # IN:     c            (-1 at end of input)
orange     0  2200   # DUP:    c c
red    -1200  2200   # PUSH 1: c c 1
green  -2400  2200   # ADD:    c c+1        (0 at end of input)
pink   -2400  1000   # BRANCH: >0 turn left to white, 0 straight on to brown
white  -1200  1000   # OUT:    writes c, then straight on to black again
brown  -2400  -200   # DROP the -1; dead end, halt
